.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt UNAME 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uname
.Nd print system and compiled release identity
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a | Fl r | Fl s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no arguments or
.Fl s ,
print
.Ql ABSD .
.Fl r
prints this program's compiled release id.
.Fl a
prints system name, compiled release id, architecture, Rust target
.Ql x86_64-unknown-absd ,
and this process's kernel PID.
ABSD has no host name to report.
Only the first argument is examined; trailing arguments are ignored.
.Pp
Commands in the selected release normally share that release's id.
For the release currently served by the file server itself, use
.Xr release 1 .
No authority or configuration changes result.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for a recognized first argument or none; 2 for an unknown first
argument, diagnosed on standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uname -a
uname -r
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr release 1 ,
.Xr process 7
